ervation namespace, the ConfigMap should also be there. So checking its existence is the first step. If it\'s not there, the solution would be to create it. If it is there, maybe the pod needs to be restarted or there\'s another issue. \n\nSo the tool call should be to check the existence of the ConfigMap. That\'s the logical next step to confirm the missing ConfigMap.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The `mongodb-geo` pod is failing due to a missing ConfigMap `mongo-geo-script` as indicated by the `FailedMount` event. To confirm this, I need to check if the ConfigMap exists in the `hotel-reservation` namespace. If it is missing, this would explain the mount failure and is a clear root cause. Running `kubectl get configmap mongo-geo-script -n hotel-reservation` will verify its presence.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=427, prompt_tokens=5115, total_tokens=5542, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc6d-7398-7783-a05e-366ac5927156-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5115, 'output_tokens': 427, 'total_tokens': 5542}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='3c55e30c-dde2-4515-991b-d54d716047f3')]]
